examples.question_text:
The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown for $0\le x\le4$. State its global maximum and global minimum values.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle,axis line style={black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},xmin=-0.4,xmax=4.5,ymin=-9,ymax=15,xtick={0,1,2,3,4},ytick={-8,-4,0,4,8,12},width=7cm,height=6cm,clip=false]
\addplot[black,thick,domain=0:4,samples=120] {8+3*x*x-x*x*x};
\addplot[black,only marks,mark=*] coordinates {(0,8) (4,-8)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Compare the heights across the whole displayed domain. The highest point is $(2,12)$, so the global maximum value is $12$. The lowest point is the included right endpoint $(4,-8)$, so the global minimum value is $-8$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle,axis line style={black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},xmin=-0.4,xmax=4.8,ymin=-11,ymax=15,xtick={0,1,2,3,4},ytick={-8,-4,0,4,8,12},width=7cm,height=6cm,clip=false]
\addplot[black,thick,domain=0:4,samples=120] {8+3*x*x-x*x*x};
\addplot[black,only marks,mark=*] coordinates {(0,8) (2,12) (4,-8)};
\path (axis cs:2,12) node[above,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] {$(2,12)$};
\path (axis cs:4,-8) node[below left,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] {$(4,-8)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
